  "title": "Mary L Possible NDE 6676",
  "date": "8-15-2007",
  "content": "I had a three hundred sixty degree fusion and the doctors nicked my femoral artery in my abdomen. When they took me to my room to hook me up to the machines, they sat me up and I became extremely tired that I couldn't keep my eyes open. This happened a few separate times. I don't know which time it was that this happened. I remember watching people running into my room from my lower left (which is odd because my feet were facing the door to my room). I remember watching this Asian male doctor and this other young male that reminded me of Joey, from the show Friends. They were leaning against a counter or wall. A nurse came into the room and the Asian man asked the nurse about how long it would be for the other two units? The nurse told him that it would be about eight minutes. He then said, ‘she needed them about eight minutes ago!’ This told me that he was in charge! I couldn't see who all these people were talking about because there were too many of them around the head of the bed giving cardiopulmonary resuscitation and talking and relaying different stats to the Doctors. It all seemed like it wasn't real, like it was a movie or something. Next thing I remember is that I was being wheeled down the hallway on a gurney, and I was in extreme pain. I believe this was when they took me to the intensive care unit.",
